The BLE device name `"Matter"` was hardcoded in three separate places in `ble_adapter.cpp`, making it fragile to rename.

## Changes

- Added `#define BLE_DEVICE_NAME "Matter"` in the constants section alongside the other `BLE_CAPS_*` defines
- Replaced all three scattered literals with `BLE_DEVICE_NAME`:
  - GAP Device Name characteristic value in `ble_adapter_init()`
  - Name pointer and `sizeof` expression in `build_scan_response()`

```c
/* Before — same string in 3 places */
const char *name = "Matter";
uint8_t name_len = (uint8_t)(sizeof("Matter") - 1);
// ...
static const uint8_t device_name[] = "Matter";

/* After — single source of truth */
