Blog post text used a fixed `line-height: 1.7rem` (27.2px), causing lines to feel cramped — especially on narrow viewports where Japanese text wraps frequently.

### Changes

- **`p` line-height**: `1.7rem` → unitless `1.9` (scales with font-size instead of being fixed)
- **`li` line-height**: Added `1.9` — list items previously had no explicit line-height
- **Removed `@media (max-width: 600px)` override**: Unitless value provides consistent proportional spacing at all widths, so the breakpoint-specific bump to `2rem` is unnecessary

```css
/* Before */
p {
  margin: 0 0 1.7rem;
  line-height: 1.7rem;
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    line-height: 2rem;
  }
}

/* After */
p {
  margin: 0 0 1.7rem;
  line-height: 1.9;
}
li {
  line-height: 1.9;
}
```

