The main `paypalac.php` module migrates old `PAYPALR_%` config values on install, but the six sub-modules do not. Installing any sub-module after upgrading from `paypalr_*` loses all existing configuration.

### Changes

- Added migration logic to `install()` in all sub-modules: `paypalac_applepay`, `paypalac_creditcard`, `paypalac_googlepay`, `paypalac_paylater`, `paypalac_savedcard`, `paypalac_venmo`
- Each sub-module SELECTs its old `MODULE_PAYMENT_PAYPALR_{SUBMODULE}_%` keys and UPDATEs the corresponding `MODULE_PAYMENT_PAYPALAC_{SUBMODULE}_%` keys, matching the existing pattern in `paypalac.php`
- Added `SubModuleMigrationTest.php` covering all six modules

Migration block added to each sub-module's `install()`, between the config INSERT and `tableCheckup()`:

```php
$old_config = $db->Execute(
    "SELECT configuration_key, configuration_value
       FROM " . TABLE_CONFIGURATION . "
      WHERE configuration_key LIKE 'MODULE\_PAYMENT\_PAYPALR\_VENMO\_%'"
);
while (!$old_config->EOF) {
    $old_key = $old_config->fields['configuration_key'];
    $new_key = str_replace('MODULE_PAYMENT_PAYPALR_VENMO_', 'MODULE_PAYMENT_PAYPALAC_VENMO_', $old_key);
    $old_value = $old_config->fields['configuration_value'];
    $db->Execute(
        "UPDATE " . TABLE_CONFIGURATION . "
            SET configuration_value = '" . zen_db_input($old_value) . "'
          WHERE configuration_key = '" . zen_db_input($new_key) . "'
          LIMIT 1"
    );
    $old_config->MoveNext();
}
```

